Let's solve this step by step.

**1. Calculate the initial volume of the aquarium before Nancy came back.**

First, we find the volume using the formula for a rectangular prism: $\text{Volume} = \text{length} \times \text{width} \times \text{height}$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Initial Volume} &= 4 \, \text{ft} \times 6 \, \text{ft} \times 3 \, \text{ft} \\
\text{Initial Volume} &= 72 \, \text{cubic feet}
\end{aligned}
$$

**2. Apply the first change (halfing the water).**

Nancy filled the aquarium halfway, removing half of its total volume.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Half Volume} &= \frac{72}{2} \\
\text{Half Volume} &= 36 \, \text{cubic feet}
\end{aligned}
$$

**3. Apply the second change (tripling the remaining water).**

Now Nancy times the amount of water by 3.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{New Volume} &= 36 \times 3 \\
\text{New Volume} &= 108 \, \text{cubic feet}
\end{aligned}
$$

The answer is: 108
